-[size=sm]:[--card-spacing:--spacing(3)] data-[size=sm]:has-data-[slot=card-footer]:pb-0 *:[img:first-child]:rounded-t-xl *:[img:last-child]:rounded-b-xl rounded-[var(--wagyu-card-radius)] bg-surface text-foreground shadow-sm ring-1 ring-inset ring-border-subtle gap-5 p-5 sm:p-6" data-page-section="center" data-page-panel="true"><div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-0 px-0"><div class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="size-5 text-input-placeholder"><path d="M13.3003 2.38913C12.4576 2.09946 11.5424 2.09946 10.6997 2.38913L5.02476 4.33988C3.81336 4.7563 3 5.89596 3 7.17694V11.9119C3 14.7187 4.14891 16.7414 5.8125 18.3163C7.38493 19.805 9.44484 20.9158 11.3681 21.9529L11.5252 22.0376C11.8215 22.1975 12.1785 22.1975 12.4748 22.0376L12.6319 21.9529C14.5552 20.9158 16.6151 19.805 18.1875 18.3163C19.8511 16.7414 21 14.7187 21 11.9119V7.17694C21 5.89596 20.1866 4.7563 18.9752 4.33988L13.3003 2.38913Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg><h2 class="text-[22px] font-black text-foreground dark:text-white">Why swap Monero on Wagyu</h2></div></div><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-pretty text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground [&amp;_strong]:font-extrabold [&amp;_strong]:text-foreground [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-3 [&amp;_ul]:pl-5 [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal [&amp;_ol]:space-y-4 [&amp;_ol]:pl-5 [&amp;_li::marker]:font-extrabold [&amp;_li::marker]:text-primary"><p>Wagyu is a private Monero swap and exchange. Send a supported asset such as Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana, USDT or USDC and receive XMR at your own address. Choose source and destination networks in the token picker. Refunds follow the published compliance policy. Screening happens before execution and may run again during recovery or refunds.</p></div><div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><div class="rounded-[var(--wagyu-panel-radius)] bg-card flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3 p-4 sm:col-span-2"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5 text-primary"><path d="M13.3003 2.38913C12.4576 2.09946 11.5424 2.09946 10.6997 2.38913L5.02476 4.33988C3.81336 4.7563 3 5.89596 3 7.17694V11.9119C3 14.7187 4.14891 16.7414 5.8125 18.3163C7.38493 19.805 9.44484 20.9158 11.3681 21.9529L11.5252 22.0376C11.8215 22.1975 12.1785 22.1975 12.4748 22.0376L12.6319 21.9529C14.5552 20.9158 16.6151 19.805 18.1875 18.3163C19.8511 16.7414 21 14.7187 21 11.9119V7.17694C21 5.89596 20.1866 4.7563 18.9752 4.33988L13.3003 2.38913Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg><h3 class="text-base font-extrabold leading-6 tracking-tight text-foreground">Screening and refund rules are published</h3><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-pretty text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground [&amp;_strong]:font-extrabold [&amp;_strong]:text-foreground [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-3 [&amp;_ul]:pl-5 [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal [&amp;_ol]:space-y-4 [&amp;_ol]:pl-5 [&amp;_li::marker]:font-extrabold [&amp;_li::marker]:text-primary"><p>Address and transaction screening runs before execution and can run again during recovery or refunds. A failed check normally enters a refund flow, which can require a refund address and further checks. The published compliance policy describes legal restrictions, including court and authorised-government orders.</p><p><a class="rounded-sm font-extrabold text-primary underline decoration-primary/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-focus-ring" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://docs.wagyu.xyz/compliance-policy">Read the full compliance policy →</a></p></div></div><div class="rounded-[var(--wagyu-panel-radius)] bg-card flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3 p-4"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5 text-primary"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M12 2C17.5228 2 22 6.47715 22 12C22 17.5228 17.5228 22 12 22C6.47715 22 2 17.5228 2 12C2 6.47715 6.47715 2 12 2ZM15.5586 8.1709C15.1005 7.8626 14.4794 7.98355 14.1709 8.44141L10.4727 13.9336L8.70703 12.168C8.31651 11.7774 7.68349 11.7774 7.29297 12.168C6.90244 12.5585 6.90244 13.1915 7.29297 13.582L9.91797 16.207C10.1293 16.4183 10.4243 16.5239 10.7217 16.4951C11.0188 16.4662 11.2873 16.3062 11.4541 16.0586L15.8291 9.55859C16.1374 9.10055 16.0165 8.47937 15.5586 8.1709Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg><h3 class="text-base font-extrabold leading-6 tracking-tight text-foreground">Track your swap or refund</h3><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-pretty text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground [&amp;_strong]:font-extrabold [&amp;_strong]:text-foreground [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-3 [&amp;_ul]:pl-5 [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal [&amp;_ol]:space-y-4 [&amp;_ol]:pl-5 [&amp;_li::marker]:font-extrabold [&amp;_li::marker]:text-primary"><p>A Monero swap on Wagyu needs one thing: the address where you want to receive your coins. Your deposit is either swapped or returned to you, subject to the compliance policy and applicable legal restrictions. Each order gets a private session key so you can track it and, if needed, submit a refund address.</p></div></div><div class="rounded-[var(--wagyu-panel-radius)] bg-card flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3 p-4"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5 text-primary"><path d="M4 11C4.55228 11 5 11.4477 5 12C5 15.866 8.13401 19 12 19C13.9107 19 15.673 18.2336 16.9531 17H15.0117C14.4594 17 14.0117 16.5523 14.0117 16C14.0117 15.4477 14.4594 15 15.0117 15H19.0117C19.564 15 20.0117 15.4477 20.0117 16V20C20.0117 20.5523 19.564 21 19.0117 21C18.4594 21 18.0117 20.5523 18.0117 20V18.7451C16.4015 20.1501 14.2809 21 12 21C7.02944 21 3 16.9706 3 12C3 11.4477 3.44772 11 4 11Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M18 4C18.2409 4 18.4574 4.1482 18.5439 4.37305L19.2402 6.18555C19.3418 6.44944 19.5506 6.65819 19.8145 6.75977L21.627 7.45605C21.8518 7.5426 22 7.75906 22 8C22 8.24094 21.8518 8.4574 21.627 8.54395L19.8145 9.24023C19.5506 9.34181 19.3418 9.55056 19.2402 9.81445L18.5439 11.627C18.4574 11.8518 18.2409 12 18 12C17.7591 12 17.5426 11.8518 17.4561 11.627L16.7598 9.81445C16.6582 9.55056 16.4494 9.34181 16.1855 9.24023L14.373 8.54395C14.1482 8.4574 14 8.24094 14 8C14 7.75906 14.1482 7.5426 14.373 7.45605L16.1855 6.75977C16.4494 6.65819 16.6582 6.44944 16.7598 6.18555L17.4561 4.37305C17.5426 4.1482 17.7591 4 18 4Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M12 3C12.5523 3 13 3.44772 13 4C13 4.55228 12.5523 5 12 5C10.0891 5 8.32687 5.76633 7.04688 7H9C9.55228 7 10 7.44772 10 8C10 8.55228 9.55228 9 9 9H5C4.44772 9 4 8.55228 4 8V4C4 3.44772 4.44772 3 5 3C5.55228 3 6 3.44772 6 4V5.24414C7.60878 3.84548 9.72476 3 12 3Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg><h3 class="text-base font-extrabold leading-6 tracking-tight text-foreground">Orderbook rates, not spread-padded quotes</h3><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-pretty text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground [&amp;_strong]:font-extrabold [&amp;_strong]:text-foreground [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-3 [&amp;_ul]:pl-5 [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal [&amp;_ol]:space-y-4 [&amp;_ol]:pl-5 [&amp;_li::marker]:font-extrabold [&amp;_li::marker]:text-primary"><p>Wagyu routes XMR trades through Hyperliquid&#x27;s decentralized orderbook. Large orders use TWAP execution: the swap is sliced and filled over time instead of being dumped in one block, which keeps slippage low. Rates are designed to match or beat centralized exchanges, and the quote you see shows the public fees and the estimated output before you send anything. The deposit amount is exact; the final output can move with the market during execution.</p></div></div><div class="rounded-[var(--wagyu-panel-radius)] bg-card flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3 p-4"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5 text-primary"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M8.5 2C10.7961 2 12.6887 3.71982 12.9639 5.94141L15.2607 6.17188C15.7838 4.89747 17.0371 4 18.5 4C20.433 4 22 5.567 22 7.5C22 9.433 20.433 11 18.5 11L18.4941 10.999L17.7178 13.585C19.0802 14.3584 20 15.8213 20 17.5C20 19.9853 17.9853 22 15.5 22C13.2039 22 11.3103 20.2802 11.0352 18.0586L8.7373 17.8291C8.21386 19.1027 6.9623 20 5.5 20C3.567 20 2 18.433 2 16.5C2 14.567 3.567 13 5.5 13H5.50488L6.28125 10.4141C4.91941 9.64042 4 8.17818 4 6.5C4 4.01472 6.01472 2 8.5 2ZM10.0117 10.7383C9.53911 10.9069 9.03051 11 8.5 11C8.39823 11 8.29735 10.9949 8.19727 10.9883L7.42188 13.5752C8.19661 14.0853 8.75594 14.8945 8.93652 15.8389L11.2334 16.0684C11.4543 15.4097 11.823 14.819 12.3008 14.3359L10.0117 10.7383ZM12.7656 7.93164C12.5447 8.59022 12.1759 9.18011 11.6982 9.66309L13.9873 13.2607C14.4601 13.092 14.9693 13 15.5 13C15.6014 13 15.702 13.0041 15.8018 13.0107L16.5781 10.4248C15.8036 9.91487 15.2443 9.10602 15.0635 8.16211L12.7656 7.93164Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg><h3 class="text-base font-extrabold leading-6 tracking-tight text-foreground">Decentralized routing across networks</h3><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-pretty text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground [&amp;_strong]:font-extrabold [&amp;_strong]:text-foreground [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-3 [&amp;_ul]:pl-5 [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal [&amp;_ol]:space-y-4 [&amp;_ol]:pl-5 [&amp;_li::marker]:font-extrabold [&amp;_li::marker]:text-primary"><p>Cross-chain legs go through a decentralized bridge aggregator, the XMR leg through Hyperliquid&#x27;s orderbook.<!-- -->The catalogue lists deposits from <!-- -->Monero, Zcash, Ethereum, Arbitrum, Base, BSC, HyperEVM, Robinhood Chain, Arc, Solana, Bitcoin, Tron<!-- --> and delivery to <!-- -->Monero, Zcash, Ethereum, Arbitrum, Base, BSC, HyperEVM, Robinhood Chain, Arc, Solana, Bitcoin, Tron, Hyperliquid, Sui<!-- -->. Catalogue fetched <!-- -->Oct 9, 2026, 7:04 AM UTC<!-- -->. Availability depends on the specific token and route; the quote checks your selection.</p></div></div><div class="rounded-[var(--wagyu-panel-radius)] bg-card flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3 p-4"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5 text-primary"><path d="M1.31226 13.3968C1.31226 10.2902 3.72572 7.77181 6.70288 7.77181C9.68002 7.77181 12.0935 10.2902 12.0935 13.3968C12.0935 16.5034 9.68002 19.0218 6.70288 19.0218C3.72572 19.0218 1.31226 16.5034 1.31226 13.3968Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M13.0918 1.10515C16.0689 1.10515 18.4824 3.62355 18.4824 6.73015C18.4824 9.64481 16.358 12.0416 13.6368 12.3267C13.4487 12.3465 13.3547 12.3563 13.2809 12.3004C13.2071 12.2445 13.1845 12.1367 13.1393 11.9213C12.5918 9.30873 10.6206 7.25186 8.11691 6.68053C7.91044 6.63341 7.80721 6.60986 7.75362 6.5328C7.70002 6.45573 7.70946 6.35763 7.72835 6.16142C8.00157 3.32191 10.2986 1.10515 13.0918 1.10515Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M4.92556 3.59864L5.55791 4.39177C5.68724 4.55399 5.88629 4.63716 6.08717 4.61291C6.28805 4.58867 6.46365 4.4603 6.55408 4.27156L7.23861 2.84299C7.33144 2.64925 7.32152 2.41916 7.21239 2.2349C7.10325 2.05064 6.91046 1.93848 6.70288 1.93848C6.07393 1.93848 5.46904 2.0508 4.90642 2.25788C2.81175 3.02884 1.31226 5.11095 1.31226 7.56348C1.31226 7.90866 1.58042 8.18848 1.91121 8.18848C2.24201 8.18848 2.51017 7.90866 2.51017 7.56348C2.51017 5.80811 3.49729 4.29582 4.92556 3.59864Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M14.869 16.5283L14.2367 15.7351C14.1074 15.573 13.9083 15.4898 13.7075 15.5141C13.5065 15.5383 13.331 15.6666 13.2405 15.8554L12.556 17.284C12.4631 17.4777 12.4731 17.7078 12.5822 17.8921C12.6914 18.0763 12.8842 18.1885 13.0917 18.1885C13.7206 18.1885 14.3256 18.0761 14.8882 17.8691C16.9829 17.0981 18.4824 15.016 18.4824 12.5635C18.4824 12.2183 18.2142 11.9385 17.8834 11.9385C17.5526 11.9385 17.2844 12.2183 17.2844 12.5635C17.2844 14.3188 16.2974 15.8311 14.869 16.5283Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg><h3 class="text-base font-extrabold leading-6 tracking-tight text-foreground">Built for Monero users, at Monero scale</h3><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-pretty text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground [&amp;_strong]:font-extrabold [&amp;_strong]:text-foreground [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-3 [&amp;_ul]:pl-5 [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal [&amp;_ol]:space-y-4 [&amp;_ol]:pl-5 [&amp;_li::marker]:font-extrabold [&amp;_li::marker]:text-primary"><p>Total volume through Wagyu is <!-- -->$1.0B+<!-- -->, including legacy swaps and bridges, as on Points. Current-engine totals include swap, bridge and coinflip orders. Updated <!-- -->Oct 9, 2026, 7:04 AM UTC<!-- -->; legacy volume as of <!-- -->Oct 9, 2026, 7:00 AM UTC<!-- -->.<!-- --> Wagyu also runs the native XMR to XMR1 bridge that brings Monero onto Hyperliquid. Monero is the first asset in the catalog, not an afterthought. Zcash swaps pay out to your shielded u1 address by default.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section id="how-h" aria-label="How a Monero swap works"><div data-slot="card" data-size="default" class="group/card flex flex-col overflow-hidden text-sm [--card-spacing:--spacing(4)] has-data-[slot=card-footer]:pb-0 has-[&gt;img:first-child]:pt-0 data-[size=sm]:[--card-spacing:--spacing(3)] data-[size=sm]:has-data-[slot=card-footer]:pb-0 *:[img:first-child]:rounded-t-xl *:[img:last-child]:rounded-b-xl rounded-[var(--wagyu-card-radius)] bg-surface text-foreground shadow-sm ring-1 ring-inset ring-border-subtle gap-5 p-5 sm:p-6" data-page-section="center" data-page-panel="true"><div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-0 px-0"><div class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="size-5 text-input-placeholder"><path d="M11 3H15.2413C16.0463 2.99999 16.7106 2.99998 17.2518 3.0442C17.8139 3.09012 18.3306 3.18868 18.816 3.43598C19.5686 3.81947 20.1805 4.43139 20.564 5.18404C20.8113 5.66938 20.9099 6.18608 20.9558 6.74818C21 7.28937 21 7.95372 21 8.75868V9H11V3Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M9 3H8.7587C7.95375 2.99999 7.28936 2.99998 6.74818 3.0442C6.18608 3.09012 5.66938 3.18868 5.18404 3.43598C4.43139 3.81947 3.81947 4.43139 3.43598 5.18404C3.18868 5.66938 3.09012 6.18608 3.0442 6.74818C2.99998 7.28936 2.99999 7.95371 3 8.75867V9H9V3Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M3 11V15.2413C2.99999 16.0463 2.99998 16.7106 3.0442 17.2518C3.09012 17.8139 3.18868 18.3306 3.43598 18.816C3.81947 19.5686 4.43139 20.1805 5.18404 20.564C5.66938 20.8113 6.18608 20.9099 6.74818 20.9558C7.28937 21 7.95372 21 8.75868 21H9V11H3Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M11 21H15.2413C16.0463 21 16.7106 21 17.2518 20.9558C17.8139 20.9099 18.3306 20.8113 18.816 20.564C19.5686 20.1805 20.1805 19.5686 20.564 18.816C20.8113 18.3306 20.9099 17.8139 20.9558 17.2518C21 16.7106 21 16.0463 21 15.2413V11H11V21Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg><h2 class="text-[22px] font-black text-foreground dark:text-white">How a Monero swap works</h2></div></div><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-pretty text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground [&amp;_strong]:font-extrabold [&amp;_strong]:text-foreground [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-3 [&amp;_ul]:pl-5 [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal [&amp;_ol]:space-y-4 [&amp;_ol]:pl-5 [&amp;_li::marker]:font-extrabold [&amp;_li::marker]:text-primary"><ol><li><strong>Choose your pair and amount</strong><p>Pick what you send and what you receive, for example BTC to XMR, and enter the amount. You get a live quote with the rate, the fee, the estimated output and the estimated time.</p></li><li><strong>Send to the one-time deposit address</strong><p>Wagyu creates a durable order with a deposit address and an exact amount. Send from any wallet; no connection required.</p></li><li><strong>Track the order</strong><p>The order page shows each stage: confirming your deposit, routing, trading on the orderbook, sending. You can keep the page open or come back later with your order link.</p></li><li><strong>Receive XMR at your address</strong><p>The coins land directly in the wallet you specified. Nothing stays on Wagyu.</p></li></ol></div><div class="rounded-[var(--wagyu-panel-radius)] bg-card flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3 p-4"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5 text-primary"><path d="M14.5634 13.5799C14.6 13.2593 14.4292 12.9316 14.1078 12.9024C14.102 12.9019 14.0961 12.9014 14.0903 12.9009L9.19669 12.5131C8.65686 12.4704 8.11351 12.5323 7.5996 12.6952L3.69783 13.932C3.28233 14.0637 3 14.4494 3 14.8852V20.0199C3 20.5721 3.44772 21.0199 4 21.0199H4.83831L4.85056 21.0237C4.95989 21.0574 5.11685 21.1047 5.31199 21.1604C5.70161 21.2716 6.24688 21.4174 6.87145 21.5561C8.09069 21.8267 9.72522 22.0966 11.0994 21.9661C12.5697 21.8264 14.3876 21.1358 15.958 20.4236C17.5608 19.6966 19.0337 18.8864 19.8515 18.4189C20.5815 18.0016 21 17.2562 21 16.472C21 14.9261 19.557 14.5558 18 15L15.5 15.75C14.5 17 13.9507 17.3157 12.3751 17.6528L11.1171 17.922C10.7369 18.0033 10.3614 17.7659 10.2718 17.3875C10.1795 16.9975 10.426 16.6078 10.8179 16.5239L12.0458 16.2612C13.4015 15.9711 14.4132 14.8936 14.5634 13.5799Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M18 7.5C18 9.433 16.433 11 14.5 11C12.567 11 11 9.433 11 7.5C11 5.567 12.567 4 14.5 4C16.433 4 18 5.567 18 7.5Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M9.20355 8.98762C9.07093 8.51447 9 8.01551 9 7.5C9 5.48869 10.0796 3.72953 11.691 2.77044C11.0912 2.28843 10.3293 2 9.5 2C7.567 2 6 3.567 6 5.5C6 7.33315 7.4093 8.83714 9.20355 8.98762Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg><h3 class="text-base font-extrabold leading-6 tracking-tight text-foreground">If something goes wrong</h3><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-pretty text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground [&amp;_strong]:font-extrabold [&amp;_strong]:text-foreground [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-3 [&amp;_ul]:pl-5 [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal [&amp;_ol]:space-y-4 [&amp;_ol]:pl-5 [&amp;_li::marker]:font-extrabold [&amp;_li::marker]:text-primary"><p>If something goes wrong, for example a deposit sent on the wrong chain or a route that becomes unavailable, the order switches to a refund state and asks you for a refund address. You never have to open a ticket to get your money back.</p></div></div></div></section><section id="to-h" aria-label="Swap any asset to Monero"><div data-slot="card" data-size="default" class="group/card flex flex-col overflow-hidden text-sm [--card-spacing:--spacing(4)] has-data-[slot=card-footer]:pb-0 has-[&gt;img:first-child]:pt-0 data-[size=sm]:[--card-spacing:--spacing(3)] data-[size=sm]:has-data-[slot=card-footer]:pb-0 *:[img:first-child]:rounded-t-xl *:[img:last-child]:rounded-b-xl rounded-[var(--wagyu-card-radius)] bg-surface text-foreground shadow-sm ring-1 ring-inset ring-border-subtle gap-5 p-5 sm:p-6" data-page-section="center" data-page-panel="true"><div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-0 px-0"><div class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="size-5 text-input-placeholder"><path d="M1.31226 13.3968C1.31226 10.2902 3.72572 7.77181 6.70288 7.77181C9.68002 7.77181 12.0935 10.2902 12.0935 13.3968C12.0935 16.5034 9.68002 19.0218 6.70288 19.0218C3.72572 19.0218 1.31226 16.5034 1.31226 13.3968Z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M13.0918 1.10515C16.0689 1.10515 18.4824 3.62355 18.4824 6.73015C18.4824 9.64481 16.358 12.0416 13.6368 12.3267C13.4487 12.3465 13.3547 12.3563 13.2809 12.3004C13.2071 12.2445 13.1845 12.1367 13.1393 11.9213C12.5918 9.30873 10.6206 7.25186 8.11691 6.68053C7.91044 6.63341 7.80721 6.60986 7.75362 6.5328C7.70002 6.45573 7.70946 6.35763 7.72835 6.16142C8.00157 3.32191 10.2986 1.10515 13.0918 1.10515Z" fill="currentColor"><